{"ticker":"BEL","symbol":"BEL","instrumentId":3022357,"name":"Bharat Electronics","industry":"NSE-Aerospace/Defense","about":"Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL), provides state-of-the-art electronic systems to empower India's armed forces. BEL produces a wide range of products, including radars, missile systems, electronic warfare, and communication systems. The company emphasizes the \"Make in India\" initiative by focusing on in-house R&D, indigenization, and partnerships with private industries. BEL is expanding its global presence, with marketing offices in Oman, Vietnam, Sri Lanka, and the USA, while also increasing its focus on civilian sectors like civil aviation, cybersecurity, and smart cities. BEL is a Navratna PSU with a strong commitment to innovation and self-reliance.","website":"www.bel-india.in","location":"Bangalore, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:08:45.980Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":404.2,"changePct":2.1222839818089887,"week52High":468.45,"week52Low":362},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹2,95,461 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹30,253 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"3,581,791,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"1,096"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"2,840,914,060"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.62%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"12.32"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.2"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.01"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.02"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"25%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"46.19"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"20–57"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"25.3%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"2.11"},{"label":"Volume","value":"4,449,384"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"10,454,987"},{"label":"Master score","value":"53"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"79"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"52"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"69"},{"label":"Acc/Dis rating","value":"B+"}],"ea